I would also add that it's quite easy to protect yourself to some extend
- one idea is to carry a light source (so that you see the corridor a few 
steps ahead), another is not to get rid of your pet too early - I almost
invariably bump into eyes in corridors (you know, one-two keys typeahead
to go faster :-) and thus can be attacked by other monsters from one direction
only. If my pet is behind me, he's often able to defend me long
enough for the paralysis to wear off... I don't mention reflection because
it is difficult to get early - but the pet idea is available to everybody
except those people 'annoyed by pets' - serves them right!
